[§ 1026.9 Subsequent disclosure requirements.] (3)(i) Disclosure requirements for rate increases —(A) General. If a creditor is increasing the rate due to delinquency or default or as a penalty, the creditor must provide the following information on the notice sent pursuant to paragraph (g)(1) of this section:
[§ 1026.9 Subsequent disclosure requirements.] ( 1 ) A statement that the delinquency or default rate or penalty rate, as applicable, has been triggered;
[§ 1026.9 Subsequent disclosure requirements.] ( 2 ) The date on which the delinquency or default rate or penalty rate will apply;
[§ 1026.9 Subsequent disclosure requirements.] ( 3 ) The circumstances under which the delinquency or default rate or penalty rate, as applicable, will cease to apply to the consumer's account, or that the delinquency or default rate or penalty rate will remain in effect for a potentially indefinite time period;
[§ 1026.9 Subsequent disclosure requirements.] ( 4 ) A statement indicating to which balances the delinquency or default rate or penalty rate will be applied;
[§ 1026.9 Subsequent disclosure requirements.] ( 5 ) If applicable, a description of any balances to which the current rate will continue to apply as of the effective date of the rate increase, unless a consumer fails to make a minimum periodic payment within 60 days from the due date for that payment; and
